{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1321884-aquiring-pathos-in-wraith-20th","id":1321884,"title":"Aquiring Pathos in Wraith 20th","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-02T09:26:05-07:00","id":1321884,"title":"Aquiring Pathos in Wraith 20th","content":"Hi everyone,<br /> <br /> Can someone tell me where in Wraith 20th it is explained how a Wraith aquires Pathos? Is it only in the section regarding Spectres and Psyche on page 382 or is there another section that explains it?<br /> <br /> Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4427-malfean_sleepover","name":"Malfean_Sleepover","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4427_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T11:11:39-07:00","id":1321894,"title":"","content":"For gaining Pathos via Passions, it's in the Passions section (Wr20, p. 305).<br /> <br /> If it's for Memoriam, that's under its Background write-up (Wr20, p 144).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T15:08:32-07:00","id":1327079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1321884-aquiring-pathos-in-wraith-20th?p=1321894#post1321894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For gaining Pathos via Passions, it's in the Passions section (Wr20, p. 305).<br /> <br /> If it's for Memoriam, that's under its Background write-up (Wr20, p 144).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4427-malfean_sleepover","name":"Malfean_Sleepover","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4427_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T06:42:02-07:00","id":1338613,"title":"","content":"I have a question too: if my passion is &quot;protect my son (love)&quot; I obviously gain pathos every time I protect my son. But what about my other actions driven by love? They're useless for pathos?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T08:09:00-07:00","id":1338631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1321884-aquiring-pathos-in-wraith-20th?p=1338613#post1338613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question too: if my passion is &quot;protect my son (love)&quot; I obviously gain pathos every time I protect my son. But what about my other actions driven by love? They're useless for pathos?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not useless, although the core book does not actually explain this. Here is a quote from Handbook for the Recently Deceased: <br /> <br /> &quot;If your character acts in a way consistent with the core emotion at the heart<br /> of a Passion, even if they\u2019re not doing exactly what the Passion says, you can try to regain some Pathos. For example, if your Passion reads \u201cProtect My Family (Love) 5\u201d and you do something that isn\u2019t directly related to your family but is, in your opinion, done out of Love, you can petition the Storyteller for the opportunity to roll for Pathos. It\u2019s a judgement call for the Storyteller as to whether they\u2019ll allow you to do so, but as long as you don\u2019t abuse the system, it\u2019s generally pretty straightforward&quot; (HftRD 11)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2317-callishka","name":"Callishka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2317_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}